  "title": "Give closed-task generated residue one governed reconciliation entry",
  "status": "running",
  "milestone": null,
  "dependencies": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "ACC-1: Records generated by a task close, including deletions performed by the pre-commit residue cleanup, remain committable through exactly one governed route after that task is closed and its claim released.",
    "ACC-2: That route is discoverable from the refusal itself: the error names the entry and the command, so an operator is never left choosing between raw git and abandoning the residue. `git record-commit --dry-run` and its real run agree on the outcome.",
    "ACC-3: A live framework claim resolves for its owning actor whether or not a lane session is active. Both lock spellings observed above resolve, or one is made canonical and migration is automatic — in neither case may the operator have to guess.",
    "ACC-4: Both required cases are red against the reproduction above before the fix and green after, and neither names a task id, actor, or file path.",
    "ACC-5: The ATM backlog records the root cause, and the two frozen ATM-GOV-0392 records are converged through the new route as the closing demonstration — not by hand."
  ],
